55,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-30T19:04:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-01T13:06:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested on 4.4, 4.4.1 and 4.5-beta7\nOn Linux KDE Neon Wayland\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta7 - KDE neon User Edition 24.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (nvidia; 570.169) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12600KF (16 threads) - 31.18 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n\nWhen you use DisplayServer.clipboard_set_primary() the clipboard is set correctly, but when I close godot my clipboard is reverted back to what it was before. \nDisplayServer.clipboard_set() works as expected\n\nThis seams like it was the same issue. but for clipboard_set() and not clipboard_set_primary()\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/4209\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. run DisplayServer.clipboard_set_primary(\"...\")\n2. Close the game\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[clipboard-set-primary.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22060667/clipboard-set-primary.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110125/timeline","performed_via_github_a